{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>יסוף.</b> [It means] \"to cease,\" like יחדו יסופו. It is from the [binyan] of doubled [letters], for you find ל׳ in the conjugation of עלומי [עלם]. Now this passage states that Israel observed this commandment and afterward enacted it; therefore Mordecai needed Esther to write [it], because she was queen."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:32.004207285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}